{"run_id": "opencode:add-feature:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "ts_iso": "2026-10-01T14:24:06", "harness": "opencode", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "task": "add-feature", "trial": 1, "success": true, "completed": true, "error": null, "wall_time_s": 37.264, "t_env_setup_s": 0.003, "t_agent_s": 37.264, "t_checker_s": 0.228, "tokens": 2823, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_cache_read": 43608, "tokens_cache_write": 39882, "tokens_output": 2809, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "usage_raw": [{"total": 11286, "input": 4, "output": 84, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"write": 11198, "read": 0}}, {"total": 13375, "input": 2, "output": 352, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"write": 13021, "read": 0}}, {"total": 14686, "input": 2, "output": 978, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"write": 13706, "read": 0}}, {"total": 15119, "input": 2, "output": 419, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"write": 992, "read": 13706}}, {"total": 15406, "input": 2, "output": 200, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"write": 506, "read": 14698}}, {"total": 16441, "input": 2, "output": 776, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"write": 459, "read": 15204}}], "token_basis": "vendor_split", "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": null, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": null, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": null, "tokens_proxy_output": null, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_proxy_calls": null, "sampling_observed": null, "token_basis_proxy": null, "proxy_capture_truncated": null, "usage_evidence_grade": null, "usage_ranking_eligible": null, "usage_ranking_exclusion_reason": null, "tokens_fresh": 2823, "turns": 6, "cmd": ["opencode", "run", "--dir", "/tmp/bench_opencode_add-feature_8i01p9sv", "-m", "google-vertex-anthropic/claude-opus-5-5@default", "--variant", "medium", "--auto", "--format", "json", "--title", "openbench", "# Add `@include` support to miniconf\n\n`miniconf` is a small INI-style configuration parser (see `miniconf/`). It\nsupports comments, `[sections]`, `key = value` assignments, and typed values.\nIts existing test suite is under `tests/` and passes.\n\nWe need configuration files to be able to pull in other files. Add support for\nan `@include` directive to the file loader.\n\n## Directive syntax\n\nA line whose first whitespace-separated token is `@include`, followed by a\npath, includes another configuration file at that point:\n\n```\n@include logging.conf\n```\n\n## Required semantics\n\n- **Inline expansion.** An `@include` line is replaced by the full contents of\n  the referenced file, in place, as if those lines had been written where the\n  directive appears. Parsing (sections, keys, comments, value coercion) then\n  proceeds over the expanded text exactly as today.\n- **Relative paths.** The include path is resolved relative to the directory of\n  the file that contains the directive (not the process working directory).\n- **Ordering / override.** Because expansion is positional, a key assigned\n  *after* an `@include` overrides a value that the included file set for the\n  same key, and a key assigned before it is overridden by the include. This\n  follows from normal \"later assignment wins\" behavior once the file is\n  expanded.\n- **Nesting.** An included file may itself contain `@include` directives; expand\n  them recursively.\n- **Missing file.** If an include target does not exist, raise\n  `miniconf.errors.ConfigError`.\n- **Cycles.** If a file includes itself directly or transitively (a cycle),\n  raise `miniconf.errors.ConfigError` rather than looping forever.\n\nOnly `miniconf.loader.load(path)` needs to handle includes. The behavior of\nevery existing function, and of files that contain no `@include` directives,\nmust not change \u2014 the current test suite must still pass.\n\nAn example pair of files is provided in `examples/` (`service.conf` includes\n`logging.conf`) to try your implementation against.\n\n## Done when\n\n`miniconf.loader.load(path)` expands `@include` directives per the semantics\nabove, existing behavior is unchanged, and the existing test suite still\npasses.\n"], "checker_exit": 0, "exec_mode": "local", "score": 1.0, "harness_version": "1.18.3 (/home/box/.local/bin/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "workspace_changed": true, "checker_stdout": "feature 6/6, regression-groups 4/4\nSCORE: 1.0000\n", "checker_stderr": "", "checker_workspace_files": {"tests/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "tests/test_config.py": {"bytes": 770, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "60d4c4c0115da28761873909ddcd845aac74e499842a92c87f29a29ad43ef045"}, "tests/test_loader.py": {"bytes": 755, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "f5ec7ba5801854dda18cdb442bccbcfefafcbd28e41ead4997fe0bbe7c9c59d9"}, "tests/test_parser.py": {"bytes": 1203, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "ae8d8f5a8d54b75c91dbcad61e52d9f99486fd7ad5a1d1d47df8eb11a25dda60"}, "tests/test_values.py": {"bytes": 507, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "bde5103c6a30055f48a3d1e306808a9710b100a14d6f20dd697d1cbe94dd151e"}, "miniconf/__init__.py": {"bytes": 226, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "6e63742dcae4f6ba0a724938f48a08a436ca60aad5cd3da9fd5c8fea86adb917"}, "miniconf/config.py": {"bytes": 1265, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "e8779151dfad52932ac945bc93c41e2b8efb3b9c33a6683ecfc698e5584764b5"}, "miniconf/errors.py": {"bytes": 140, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "1504dc27fbd7b1938f4b4c9cf0fd932298f72437f26b00c65344fbe186f54280"}, "miniconf/loader.py": {"bytes": 2525, "mtime": 1790879067.763773, "sha256": "5146cd84c0b6386f688a77d114a015c8166c9ac7d529d58456bb2081b77c653e"}, "miniconf/parser.py": {"bytes": 1538, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "73c4203febe2e996f10387e3740aa91de2a696d743a5c4ce5855e8cf6c49c163"}, "miniconf/values.py": {"bytes": 771, "mtime": 1790809740.9319057, "sha256": "516686ad2b281d7fa3db357fdabb5fd7a51c6975e02a6d68988f7f1a474227ef"}, "examples/logging.conf": {"bytes": 86, "mtime": 179080